**Found it** — `internal/sem/types.go:918-928`:

```go
for _, flow := range flows {        // map range: order is random
    out = append(out, flow)
}
sort.Slice(out, func(i, j int) bool {
    if out[i].Name != out[j].Name { return out[i].Name < out[j].Name }
    return out[i].EvidenceKind < out[j].EvidenceKind   // tie-break STOPS here
})
```

The map is drained in random order and then sorted by `(Name, EvidenceKind)` only. Two forwarded params of the same callee share both fields and differ only in `Detail`, so they compare **equal** — and `sort.Slice` is not stable, so their order follows the random map order. `relationDedupKey` then keeps whichever landed first. Let me fix it.

