test fixture out of <span class="inst">~/go/pkg/mod</span>. carbon's tool arm read the gold regex from the
composer cache. Three of four favour the tool, so closing them will most likely make these numbers
<em>worse</em>.</p></div>

<h2>What to do next</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Close the leaks and re-measure.</strong> Nothing is quotable until then. One cell, 40 sessions.</li>
<li><strong>Run the aim discriminator.</strong> Free and offline: correlate per-instance gold-line coverage
against residual locate ops. It decides whether fixing aim is worth ~11 points or ~2 &mdash; the two available
estimates differ by 10&times;.</li>
<li><strong>Only then implement the callee hop</strong>, narrowly: enable it where the co-member fallback is
already off and the body-match signal is absent. Budget-neutral &mdash; move the window's centre, never widen it.</li>
<li><strong>Retire file coverage as a metric.</strong> It is 100% on winners and losers alike.</li>
